    "notes": "Coachman’s hut/Кучерская изба, way167382256, remains independent from Volkonsky House and the other estate houses. The exact mapped9.7m by5.5m four-sided outline fixes the axes: X northwest along the long face, Z northeast toward the photographed front approach. Native east/up/south axes are baked with heading0, using the unchanged assigned collection coordinate as model origin. Ordinary oblique pictures guide the two-window/one-door long front and one glazed short end; rear faces and absolute front assignment remain an approximate photo/map interpretation, not a survey. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m terrain; outside northeast approach provider[2.5,6] supplies215.68442192541778m datum. Original boundary grades-1.644..0.348m, floor+0.5m and closed foundation-1.85m. Coarse terrain falls about2m along this small footprint: the downhill plinth is therefore more exposed than in the photographs. The datum and broad supported foundation provide an explicitly approximate fit; no flattening or bespoke terrain. Original approach, independent neighbors, roads and ponds remain. Historic levels, thresholds and accessibility are not surveyed. Inspected native front, doorway and rear/low-side views: the whole log body, hip roof, chimney and supported entrance align with the mapped outline; the coarse slope exposes a high downhill plinth compared with the photographs. One owned map record is replaced,242 resident independent buildings and original roads/pond water remain. This explicitly approximate fit retains the unmodified standard ground. One owned map record is replaced while242 resident/294 wider independent buildings, original paths/lawn, roads and40070.675m² pond water remain. Failure retains all243 originals; every LOD/failure/unload case restores ground/water and releases geometry."
