  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Complete mapped coachman’s hut exterior at Yasnaya Polyana: single-storey log cabin with broad thick thatched hip roof, short ridge, one pale capped chimney, two front windows, one short-side window and one physically recessed wooden front door. Nearby levels add coarse log courses/corner ends, simple window bars, ridge hold-down poles and low garden edging interrupted at the supported entrance. All four actual mapped edges are retained. Hidden rear faces, chimney inventory, thatch profile and historic levels remain approximate. No interiors, copied signs, inscriptions, plaques, people, photograph pixels or surrounding plantings. Photo-led medium-fi scale:2.5m log eaves, thick2.55m thatched hip rise and one pale chimney to about6.13m above floor. Map nominal5m is a scale cue. Roof thickness, doorway/window dimensions, hold-down poles, threshold and low garden edging approximate. Retained Protomaps20261020 and Mapzen201x201/6m terrain; outside northeast approach provider[2.5,6] supplies215.68442192541778m datum. Original boundary grades-1.644..0.348m, floor+0.5m and closed foundation-1.85m. Coarse terrain falls about2m along this small footprint: the downhill plinth is therefore more exposed than in the photographs. The datum and broad supported foundation provide an explicitly approximate fit; no flattening or bespoke terrain. Original approach, independent neighbors, roads and ponds remain. Historic levels, thresholds and accessibility are not surveyed. Exact historic levels, rear bays, front assignment, thresholds and accessibility are not surveyed. Some fixed shared/style detail views crop the opposite edge; flat synthetic ground can bury grade-specific bases/treads. Whole/turntable/native views cover the envelope. The other estate models remain independent procedural context in this isolated fixture. Physical phone/laptop and dense-city timings remain pending."
  },
